{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 0, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e2b-it", "content": "Hark gentle traveler to Nippon's shore\nA journey grand a tale to explore\nFrom ancient lands to cities bright\nA fortnight's quest a wondrous sight.\n\n**Day First**\n\nArrive at Narita a land of grace\nAnd seek a lodging in Tokyo's space\nA hotel grand a bed so deep\nWhere weary limbs may softly sleep.\n\n**Day Second**\n\nExplore the Shinjuku district bold\nWith neon lights a story told\nThe gardens serene a peaceful hue\nA respite found for me and you.\n\n**Day Third**\n\nTo Asakusa we shall now proceed\nWhere Senso-ji temple plants a seed\nOf ancient faith and mystic lore\nA sacred place to evermore adore.\n\n**Day Fourth**\n\nThe Imperial Palace a regal view\nWhere emperors once did reign anew\nThrough gardens stroll with gentle pace\nA history etched upon each face.\n\n**Day Fifth**\n\nTo Hakone's hills we now shall fly\nWith Mount Fuji gleaming in the sky\nA cruise upon the lake so still\nA painter's dream a wondrous thrill.\n\n**Day Sixth**\n\nKyoto beckons a city fair\nWith temples grand beyond compare\nKinkaku-ji gold reflects the sun\nA perfect day has just begun.\n\n**Day Seventh**\n\nFushimi Inari's gates so red\nA thousand torii overhead\nA winding path a mystic climb\nTo seek enlightenment in space and time.\n\n**Day Eighth**\n\nArashiyama's bamboo grove so tall\nA verdant whisper answering all\nA tranquil scene a sweet delight\nBathed in emerald filtered light.\n\n**Day Ninth**\n\nNara's deer a curious sight\nThey bow and prostrate with all their might\nTodai-ji's Buddha a golden gaze\nA peaceful wonder in a hazy maze.\n\n**Day Tenth**\n\nOsaka's streets a vibrant scene\nDotonbori's lights a joyful sheen\nTakoyaki stalls a tasty treat\nA culinary joy both savory and sweet.\n\n**Day Eleventh**\n\nHiroshima's Peace Memorial stands\nA solemn place in hallowed lands\nA testament to peace and might\nA beacon shining ever bright.\n\n**Day Twelft